red model caches, port 7437 and prior validation directories"]},"acceptanceCriteria":["The planner records the exact clean current base and renders the affected private Current/Proposed Go shapes. The solution remains an additive, source-compatible Models transport/composition change with no public CLI, HTTP, OpenAPI, generated or persisted-data contract delta.","With a task-owned explicit INFINITE_YOU_OMNIVOICE_CACHE_DIR, a controlled public local models invoke tts populates only that root; subsequent local models list and inspect resolve the same canonical revision and report READY/INSTALLED without consulting or materializing the default profile cache.","Local models remove tts targets the same selected revision, refuses active leases, validates containment without following links, reports positive measured bytes removed, preserves unrelated cache entries and paths, and leaves list/inspect MISSING/NOT_INSTALLED. A repeated remove returns typed MODEL_CACHE_NOT_FOUND.","Empty cache selection preserves the current default-root behavior. Mixed case model names normalize consistently. Invalid, symlinked, escaping and in-use paths keep their existing typed, bounded failures with no partial or cross-root deletion.","Focused normal and race tests cover the production command-to-scope path and the controlled invoke -> list -> inspect -> remove sequence. Existing Models root-composition tests and make test pass; current-head CI is terminal green and independent review confirms no cache-format, public-contract or unsafe-cleanup regression.","The merged slice claims only the deterministic cache command coherence correction. A fresh rebuilt immutable distribution plus separate customer and engineering real TTS retests remain mandatory before LA-14/LA-15 TTS can pass."],"validationCommands":["go test ./pkg/services/models/transports/cli ./pkg/wire ./pkg/transports/cli -count=1","go test -race ./pkg/services/models/transports/cli ./pkg/wire -count=1","go test ./tests/functional