red model caches, port 7437 and prior validation directories"]},"acceptanceCriteria":["The planner records the exact clean current base and renders the affected private Current/Proposed Go shapes. The solution remains an additive, source-compatible Models transport/composition change with no public CLI, HTTP, OpenAPI, generated or persisted-data contract delta.","With a task-owned explicit INFINITE_YOU_OMNIVOICE_CACHE_DIR, a controlled public local models invoke tts populates only that root; subsequent local models list and inspect resolve the same canonical revision and report READY/INSTALLED without consulting or materializing the default profile cache.","Local models remove tts targets the same selected revision, refuses active leases, validates containment without following links, reports positive measured bytes removed, preserves unrelated cache entries and paths, and leaves list/inspect MISSING/NOT_INSTALLED. A repeated remove returns typed MODEL_CACHE_NOT_FOUND.","Empty cache selection preserves the current default-root behavior. Mixed case model names normalize consistently. Invalid, symlinked, escaping and in-use paths keep their existing typed, bounded failures with no partial or cross-root deletion.","Focused normal and race tests cover the production command-to-scope path and the controlled invoke -> list -> inspect -> remove sequence. Existing Models root-composition tests and make test pass; current-head CI is terminal green and independent review confirms no cache-format, public-contract or unsafe-cleanup regression.","The merged slice claims only the deterministic cache command coherence correction. A fresh rebuilt immutable distribution plus separate customer and engineering real TTS retests remain mandatory before LA-14/LA-15 TTS can pass."],"validationCommands":["go test ./pkg/services/models/transports/cli ./pkg/wire ./pkg/transports/cli -count=1","go test -race ./pkg/services/models/transports/cli ./pkg/wire -count=1","go test ./tests/functional/models/root_composition -count=1 -timeout 20m","go test -race ./tests/functional/models/root_composition -count=1 -timeout 30m","make test","make lint","git diff --check"],"budget":{"time":"3 hours maximum for implementation and focused local verification; ordinary CI/review lifetime thereafter","download":"0 model/backend bytes and 0 new paid/package downloads; existing Go/module caches and controlled local fixtures only","disk":"2 GiB maximum additional task-owned worktree, build, controlled cache and test output","process":"at most 4 test/build children; no heavyweight LocalAI backend and no use of port 7437","paid":"USD 0"},"failureDisposition":"Any need to change public grammar/schema, persisted cache format, model/backend identity, or files outside the owned surfaces returns to the Project lead with exact Current/Proposed evidence. Any unchanged failure is not retried. A controlled test pass cannot be promoted to real TTS acceptance; only a fresh immutable post-merge distribution and independent customer/engineering rerun can close the failed row.","parallelAssessment":{"ready":"The cache command coherence correction is the smallest cause-specific product slice and has no active implementation owner. work-task-3 is stranded at to-complete after merged delivery and is retained only as an exact cycle dependency.","compatibleSibling":"The ASR engineering validation is read-only, runs the already-qualified immutable distribution, owns a distinct fresh profile/cache/install/output tree and the sole heavyweight ASR backend window. The implementation lane makes zero real calls and does not touch validation caches, so there is no file, interface, model-memory, process or deletion collision.","waiting":"A fresh TTS customer/engineering retry waits for this correction to merge and for a new exact build/SHA-256. EMBED, text, image, video and the Factory journey remain useful but are not admitted in this batch; the next cycle reassesses them against the ASR result, current heavy-resource availability and exact fixture ownership. macOS/Linux real conformance still requires matching immutable platform artifacts and actual hosts."}}},{"workId":"batch-localai-project-cycle-081-cache-command-coherence-and-asr-engineering-20260910-localai-v3-engineering-windows-asr-known-wav-clean-install-e29f-001","name":"localai-v3-engineering-windows-asr-known-wav-clean-install-e29f-001","workTypeName":"validation","payload":{"role":"engineering","project":"localai","mission":"Independently validate the immutable Windows amd64 public distribution's real ASR journey with the pinned 10,340-byte known-speech WAV. Start from a fresh isolated environment where YOU is not installed and product configuration, state, model and backend caches are empty; install only the declared public distribution, verify exact source/build identity, and use the documented built-in asr surface. Perform one cold real ASR invocation and separate warm offline reuse, validate transcript and segments semantically and structurally, inspect Models/cache/backend ownership and LocalAI provision-start-invoke-release evidence, exercise bounded malformed/missing-input failure before heavyweight work, and attempt documented product cleanup. Record exact commands, identities, timing, network/download/disk/process use and PASS, FAIL or INCONCLUSIVE per rubric. Do not read any prior validation report, do not edit or repair files, do not reuse a prior probe cache, do not contact or mutate the Factory on port 7437, and do not advance queue state.","criteria":[{"id":"LA-03-ASR-ENGINEERING","rubric":"PASS only if an independent validator ties the installed executable to the declared clean source archive and verifies Models ownership, cache/backend selection, output shaping, LocalAI lifecycle and transport entry without repair, source drift, another validator's report or an implementation claim."},{"id":"LA-04-ASR-REAL","rubric":"PASS only if public ASR grammar and built-in resolution, cold provision/load/invoke, transcript plus segments output, separate warm offline reuse, release and bounded malformed/missing-input behavior all succeed with typed results; a missing stage, undocumented workaround or unbounded wait fails."},{"id":"LA-06-ASR-SEMANTICS","rubric":"PASS only if the WAV identity and RIFF structure match, the normalized English transcript is exactly zero, segments are structured with finite nonnegative monotonic millisecond timestamps bounded by the 644 ms fixture, and output media types, sizes and SHA-256 values are recorded; exit zero or nonempty output alone fails."},{"id":"LA-09-WINDOWS-ASR","rubric":"PASS only if the exact Windows amd64 build uses the real pinned ASR model and LocalAI Whisper backend, directly records provisioning, startup/readiness, cold and warm invocation and release, and leaves no owned process, listener, lease, partial or staging artifact; controlled fixtures cannot substitute."},{"id":"LA-10-ASR-ENGINEERING","rubric":"PASS only if exact platform/build/distribution/fixture identities, isolated roots, timeouts, process lifetime, permitted network origins, observed download and disk high-water, real-call count and USD 0 spend are recorded and remain within the declared budget."},{"id":"LA-14-ASR-ENGINEERING","rubric":"PASS only with a fresh independent engineering verdict covering provenance, installation, failure behavior, lifecycle, cache ownership, semantic ASR output and cleanup on this immutable distribution; FAIL, INCONCLUSIVE or missing evidence blocks."},{"id":"LA-15-ASR-ENGINEERING","rubric":"PASS only if absence before install, the public PowerShell install route, installed hash/build identity, cold first use without prewarmed assets, separate warm offline reuse, meaningful transcript/segments, release and complete documented product-owned cleanup are directly witnessed without hidden setup or filesystem repair."}],"reportPath":"C:/Users/andre/work/portos/infinite-you/docs/temp/projects/localai/validation/cycle-